This directory contains the source code for Zork I, a 1980 interactive fiction
game written by Marc Blank, Dave Lebling, Bruce Daniels, and Tim Anderson and
published by Infocom. In 2025, it was released as open source by Microsoft (see
the LICENSE file for details).

Zork II and III are also available as open source:
* https://github.com/historicalsource/zork2
* https://github.com/historicalsource/zork3

The Zork games were originally built with Infocom's compiler, ZILCH, but ZILF is
able to compile them without modification.

As a product of a different era, the code uses some conventions and practices
that are not recommended for use in new ZIL projects. For example, Zork predates
the concept of a "standard library" for interactive fiction, so it contains its
own copy of the entire parser, which was copied from one game to another (with
slight modifications) as new projects were started.

Much of the functionality in Zork's parser is now available as part of ZILF's
standard library, but some details of the implementation differ, so this code
may not be the best reference for how to write a new game using ZILF. It's
included here primarily for historical interest and as a demonstration of ZILF's
ability to compile legacy ZIL code.
